aduate by Hilton, Tempo by Hilton, Motto by Hilton, Hilton Hotels & Resorts, DoubleTree by Hilton, Curio Collection by Hilton, Tapestry Collection by Hilton, Outset Collection by Hilton, Embassy Suites by Hilton, Homewood Suites by Hilton, Home2 Suites by Hilton, LivSmart Studios by Hilton, Hilton Garden Inn, Hampton by Hilton, Tru by Hilton, Spark by Hilton, Hilton Grand Vacations, Small Luxury Hotels of the World, AutoCamp, and Hilton Honors brand names. The company has operations in North America, South America, and Central America, including various Caribbean nations; Europe, the Middle East, and Africa; and the Asia Pacific. Hilton Worldwide Holdings Inc. was founded in 1919 and is headquartered in McLean, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher J. Nassetta | President, CEO & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $4.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 182K people. Revenue per employee of $66K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $11K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $934 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 69\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Hilton Worldwide Holdings Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $82.3B market cap on $12.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 24% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 16-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $2.0B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.46\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 4.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 145% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 3 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.4451713629389553},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $62.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 15% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Hilton Worldwide (HLT) Up 4.7% Since Last Earnings Report: Can It Continue?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036002/hilton-worldwide-hlt-up-4-7-since-last-earnings-report-can-it-continue?cid=CS-ZC-FT-realtime_blog-3036002","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795707012.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(HLT) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/89/HLT_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_112126050001_1795298401.html","date":"2026-11-21","timestamp":1795298401.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here's How Much $1000 Invested In Hilton Worldwide Holdings 5 Years Ago Would Be Worth Today","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/11/63688585/here-s-how-much-1000-invested-hilton-worldwide-holdings-5-years-ago-would-be-worth-today","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795821313.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.226,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Q3 earnings highs and lows: United Airlines vs the rest of the consumer discretionary - travel and vacation providers stocks","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nasdaq/ual/news/earnings/q3-earnings-highs-and-lows-united-airlines-vs-the-rest-of-the-consumer-discretionary-travel-and-vacation-providers-stocks","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795750259.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.599,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Prediction: These 3 Consumer Stocks Will Beat the S&P 500 Over the Next 10 Years","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/prediction-3-consumer-stocks-beat-225002000.html","date":"2026-11-